    },
    "MODEL": {
      "status": "INCONCLUSIVE",
      "detail": "the AEi 2008 UCC28C43_STEADY macro-model contains a probable internal wiring defect that MASKES the UVLO function: STOF2 VDD 19 VDD GND SUVLO ties node 19 to the VDD control terminal through RUVLO=1MEG, so V(19) can never follow VDD. VREF/GB6/EBREF judge V(19) and therefore stay near 0V. Verified in the reproduced waveforms: at VIN=24V (VDD forced to 24V by the TI deck) VREF/RTCT ~ -0.158mV and VOUT2 ~ 0V; the OUT driver nonetheless toggles ~3.5MHz because EOut only tests V(VREF,GND)>2.5 where VREF is the DECK node (~2.5V), not the internal reference. This is a model-level finding, not a licence to edit the vendor file."
    },
    "ELECTRICAL": {
      "status": "FAIL_AS_WAVEFORMS (not as a power stage: none is present)",
      "detail": "the replayed fixture does not reproduce a plausible UCC28C43 output: no regulated 12V bias, no VREF, no UVLO hand-off; switching is a fast unlicensed toggling, not a current-mode 110kHz operation."
    },
    "POWER_STAGE": {
      "status": "NOT_EVALUATED",
      "detail": "the TI fixture has no OVP, no HV output, no 170V network, no real gate drive. Controller oscillation here is explicit evidence of nothing about the QS30-9 boost stage."
    }
